  "prompt": "Transparent PNG game art experiment sheet for TinySeaWar. First reference is Yukikaze identity; second reference is the Warspite style/layout anchor. Exactly TWO separate cutouts in two columns with a broad EMPTY transparent middle gutter, no text: LEFT a full-body 2-head-tall chibi girl WITHOUT ship/rig/weapons. RIGHT a separate simple top-down destroyer rig WITHOUT person. Match the anchor's clean bold dark-blue contours, large flat colors and minimal cel shadows, even simpler where possible; intended person display height 56px. Yukikaze identity: short warm brown bob, small upward ahoge, amber eyes, single red-white pinwheel hair ornament on her left, white sailor blouse with navy collar and red necktie, navy short skirt, ankle boots, cheerful determined expression, tiny red lucky charm. No tiny metallic accessories. Full upright body feet visible, head about half height. Separate rig: compact low gray destroyer pod, pointed bow to RIGHT, two clearly separated quadruple torpedo tube mounts and three small simple twin gun turret shapes; no railings, flags, water, wakes or detailed rivets. Muted slate gray with restrained red accent. Do not draw a full scale model ship, make a broad simple icon-like rig silhouette with readable major hardware. Both subjects fully inside canvas with generous transparent border including the rightmost bow. Person wholly left of x45%, rig wholly right of x55%. No words, labels or grid.",
